1
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:39,890
Rule one.

2
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,240
You must completely repeat the action

3
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:43,100
of your first time jump to travel.

4
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,170
Rule two.

5
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,920
You can only jump to a time

6
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:47,960
where you can fully visualize the scene in your mind.

7
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:48,759
This means

8
00:01:48,759 --> 00:01:50,680
you can only jump to an earlier timeline.

9
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,340
Rule three.

10
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:52,960
You cannot let your past self

11
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,840
know of your existence after the jump.

12
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,520
You cannot

13
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:56,880
meet yourself

14
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:58,200
face to face.

15
00:01:59,240 --> 00:01:59,600
Why?

16
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:01,200
Time paradox.

17
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,760
It would cause two time domains to overlap.

18
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,080
The timeline would collapse.

19
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,440
People would be trapped in an endless loop.

20
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:08,440
No life, no death.

21
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:09,660
Nowhere to escape.

22
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,920
Have you ever tried breaking the rules?

23
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,260
If you don't let her go look for him

24
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:37,200
and give up completely,

25
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,440
she'll be the one in trouble.

26
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:47,700
You don't know about Sophie and Mara's past, do you?

27
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:51,140
Mara was Sophie's first love.

28
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:55,360
The reason she likes you

29
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,720
is because you remind her of Mara.

30
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,980
Stop mentioning Mara.

31
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,700
If I were the one who just went out,

32
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,130
would you have looked for me

33
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,900
like crazy, just like you did?

34
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,480
Didn't I look for you?

35
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:21,450
When you suddenly left,

36
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,329
I looked for you like crazy,

37
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:26,530
afraid of any danger that might have happened to you.

38
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:32,650
Only later did I find out

39
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:36,180
that you just went abroad.

40
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:39,610
You just left without saying goodbye.

41
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,160
I didn't know whether to be happy or sad.

42
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,600
But that incident

43
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:48,500
has always weighed on my mind.

44
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:52,140
Have you forgotten it all?

45
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:56,160
For so many years,

46
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:58,690
I've had nightmares every day.

47
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,080
I can't live a normal life.

48
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:02,280
Then what could I do?

49
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:06,560
I'm really tired.

50
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,930
If my death can earn your forgiveness,

51
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:16,860
then let's wait until twelve o'clock together.

52
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,180
Do not be deceived.

53
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,440
God cannot be mocked.

54
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,210
Whatever a man sows,

55
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:33,560
that he will also reap.

56
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:54,360
Mara.

57
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:55,640
If you want revenge,

58
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,159
come and see me openly.

59
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:04,480
You had ten years to find me.

60
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,960
Why tonight?

61
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,240
In this world,

62
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:10,000
there are so many people who succeed by any means.

63
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:10,600
They don't have it.

64
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,520
They don't have their Mara.

65
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:13,120
Why am I the only one who does?

66
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,520
Don't deceive yourself.

67
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:57,960
Help!

68
00:06:58,880 --> 00:06:59,840
Help!

69
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:02,160
An'an.

70
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,160
The one who deserves to die isn't An'an,

71
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,400
nor Xiaotao.

72
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,480
It's me.

73
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:11,480
I have to go back to the past to save them.

74
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:55,120
Nine o'clock.

75
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:59,200
At this point, I had just thrown the dissected Xiaofei

76
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:00,760
onto the dining table.

77
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,320
An'an, Xiaotao, Sophie.

78
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,060
I will definitely save you this time.

79
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:21,360
Are you crazy?

80
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:23,360
You just scolded everyone upstairs

81
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,690
and dissected Xiaofei.

82
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,700
What are you doing now?

83
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:31,170
What happened to your hand?

84
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:34,640
It's nothing.

85
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,960
Seeing you guys again

86
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:40,539
is so great.

87
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:48,180
You're hugging both of us now?

88
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:49,280
If you keep acting crazy,

89
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:50,960
believe it or not, I'll hack you to death.

90
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,020
In this situation,

91
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,200
staying alive is more important.

92
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,240
Listen to me.

93
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,200
This is a typical closed-circle mystery

94
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:58,600
with a masked killer.

95
00:08:58,600 --> 00:08:59,960
They all have one thing in common.

96
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:00,800
Those who are alone die first,

97
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:01,520
and those who stick together die later.

98
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:02,880
So from now on,

99
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:04,560
we must be a tight-knit group.

100
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:05,760
Is this your new book?

101
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,960
Can you stop scaring people?

102
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:09,120
Trust me.

103
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:11,920
This is the only way we won't be in danger.

104
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:13,380
Everything I said is true.

105
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,650
What are you guys

106
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,400
doing?

107
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,820
You're still alive, Xiaotao.

108
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:28,920
That's great.
